IN THE HIGH COURT OF DELHI
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 3432 of 2020
CITATION: 2021 SCC OnLine Del 1421
YEAR: 2021

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: Pratibha M. Singh

PARTIES:
Management vs Trade Union

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Industrial Disputes Act, 1947

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 2(s) ID Act, Section 25F ID Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
workman definition, retrenchment compensation, illegal termination

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Interpreted the definition of 'workman' under Section 2(s) of Industrial Disputes Act, emphasizing the nature of primary duties rather than job designations.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 2(s) ID Act, Section 25F ID Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

